      "message": "Currently, the patch handles `EAGAIN` and `EWOULDBLOCK`, but treats all other `OSError`s as fatal, mapping them to an `EOFError`. If the script receives a non-fatal interrupt signal during the `read()` system call, it will raise `errno.EINTR` (Interrupted system call) and incorrectly assume the console disconnected.\n* **Recommendation:** Include `errno.EINTR` in the tuple of ignorable `errno`s to ensure maximum robustness.\n\n\n```python\nexcept OSError as e:\n    if e.errno in (errno.EAGAIN, errno.EWOULDBLOCK, errno.EINTR):\n        continue\n    ch \u003d b\"\"\n\n```",
